  "executive_briefing": "As of September 2026, the digital asset ecosystem approaches a historical watershed with the Senate cloture vote on the CLARITY Act (H.R. 3633) set for September 15. The bill's safe harbor provisions for non-custodial smart contracts are fueling a structural surge in native Bitcoin programmability, positioning BTC script-based dApps as direct competitors to Ethereum EVM dominance. Concurrently, spot Bitcoin ETFs remain in a Fatigue stage following 2026 net outflows and asset consolidation, shifting institutional behavior from explosive speculative inflows to static macro portfolio rebalancing. To bridge the BTC and EVM worlds, cross-chain architecture is rapidly maturing toward trust-minimized, intent-based liquidity networks that remove reliance on vulnerable wrapped-token bridges.",
